.TH MD_GET_FRAME_COUNT 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_frame_count \- query the number of processed spectrum frames
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

uint64_t md_get_frame_count(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Query the number of processed spectrum frames.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a uint64_t frame count, or zero for NULL decoder. This query has no
errno-based failure return.
.SH REMARKS
Counts completed live input hops or external-spectrum calls since construction
or reset. It does not count samples or per-channel historical replay work. A
partially filled sample hop is not counted until completed. md_flush() adds
synthetic drain frames; repeated flush adds none. Multiply by
geometry.frame_seconds to obtain the processed frame time, which includes
padding and drain silence and is not a wall-clock timestamp. Reset returns the
counter to zero.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_geometry (3),
.BR md_process_spectrum (3),
.BR md_flush (3),
.BR md_reset (3)
